1
00:00:03,573 --> 00:00:06,294
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I have some questions sent in from a friend.

2
00:00:07,474 --> 00:00:09,935
[SPEAKER_01]: He's wondering if you could answer them for him.

3
00:00:11,696 --> 00:00:15,137
[SPEAKER_01]: He says, I find myself stuck in a recurring cycle.

4
00:00:16,138 --> 00:00:25,441
[SPEAKER_01]: I act wholesomely for a while, then gradually act in minor unwholesome ways, which eventually escalate into more significant act.

5
00:00:26,898 --> 00:00:32,782
[SPEAKER_01]: Afterwards, I'm filled with regret and return to acting wholesomely, only for the pattern to repeat.

6
00:00:34,003 --> 00:00:40,588
[SPEAKER_01]: And right now, I'm in the regret stage, fully aware that I sabotaged myself intentionally.

7
00:00:41,769 --> 00:00:46,293
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel the urge to double down on my efforts to break the cycle, but that's exactly what I always do.

8
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:49,275
[SPEAKER_01]: And it never seems to lead to real progress.

9
00:00:49,835 --> 00:00:53,158
[SPEAKER_01]: How can I genuinely move forward rather than just going in circles?

10
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:55,960
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, the thing is...

11
00:00:57,610 --> 00:01:09,418
[SPEAKER_00]: As a as a householder living in already compromised environment, going in circles is a way of progressing.

12
00:01:11,579 --> 00:01:17,083
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you will not have a clean break, because you are not making a clean break from the environment.

13
00:01:18,544 --> 00:01:23,847
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's not, you know, I'm not trying to justify the failure, but I'm just saying it's inevitable.

14
00:01:29,665 --> 00:01:36,148
[SPEAKER_00]: Frustrated, in a sense of thinking, but surely I must, like, just have a, like a, like, you know, a clean determination.

15
00:01:36,168 --> 00:01:40,609
[SPEAKER_00]: They will, they will create, like, a clean sort of ending of these unwholesome states and ways of acting.

16
00:01:41,249 --> 00:01:42,090
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not going to happen.

17
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:53,234
[SPEAKER_00]: You're going to build up a determination, you're going to keep up with it, you're going to be restrained, you're going to be paying attention to the intentions behind your actions, and then you're going to fail, because you're going to start slipping, because the environment is compromising.

18
00:01:54,936 --> 00:01:58,517
[SPEAKER_00]: When you slip, the remorse, the regret, it's part of the progress.

19
00:01:58,997 --> 00:02:10,719
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's important to then not try to psychologize that away, and justify, or even worse, fall into a view that, no, I shouldn't be even trying to restrain, I shouldn't be even trying to break this vicious cycle.

20
00:02:11,459 --> 00:02:15,980
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's through going through the vicious cycle, internally, you are kind of making the effort.

21
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:24,221
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can't... unless you change your environment drastically, you will be failing, and you have to accept that you're going to feel miserable on account of it.

22
00:02:25,803 --> 00:02:33,891
[SPEAKER_00]: That will then help you build determination better, that will then help you become even more familiar with your intentions, and then you're going to fail again, and then you're going to repeat, and then you're going to fail again, and then you're going to repeat.

23
00:02:34,651 --> 00:02:41,638
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you are actually getting closer to, eh... not falling back as much as you used to.

24
00:02:44,121 --> 00:02:47,143
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, do you have time for such a practice?

25
00:02:47,924 --> 00:02:49,546
[SPEAKER_00]: How long can you sustain?

26
00:02:50,126 --> 00:02:50,587
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you have

27
00:02:51,943 --> 00:02:59,626
[SPEAKER_00]: Fifty years of that slow progress of constant failure and stuff, it might make some difference by the end of it, but it might not.

28
00:02:59,987 --> 00:03:00,947
[SPEAKER_00]: You might run out of time.

29
00:03:01,147 --> 00:03:03,048
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there is that risk as well that you have to accept.

30
00:03:03,988 --> 00:03:18,475
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you can, try and shape your environment as much as you can, so it's supporting, so that when you start slipping, you don't slip as far, because simply you don't have access to things that make you slip as far.

31
00:03:19,756 --> 00:03:20,656
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to foresee that.

32
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:28,736
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you start to notice the little things that, you know, all these minor acts that you do, that lead to this...

33
00:03:28,796 --> 00:03:29,576
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, yeah.

34
00:03:29,596 --> 00:03:30,137
[SPEAKER_01]: ...breakdown.

35
00:03:30,297 --> 00:03:30,497
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

36
00:03:31,257 --> 00:03:31,718
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you try...

37
00:03:31,738 --> 00:03:42,023
[SPEAKER_00]: They add up, add up, add up, and then, eventually, when the breakdown starts happening, you have no means of stopping it, because you already built up the momentum from before.

38
00:03:42,724 --> 00:03:46,366
[SPEAKER_00]: And honesty, the whole time, you know, the honest... like, oh, when I...

39
00:03:46,386 --> 00:03:48,267
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm watching TV,

40
00:03:49,417 --> 00:03:51,178
[SPEAKER_01]: Entertainment, breaking precepts, yeah.

41
00:03:51,338 --> 00:03:51,778
[SPEAKER_01]: And so on.

42
00:03:51,878 --> 00:03:54,360
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, where does that lead, eventually?

43
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,622
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, all of those reflections will have to be, obviously, cultivated and effected.

44
00:03:58,642 --> 00:04:03,425
[SPEAKER_00]: But the thing is, with all of that, as I said, the environment is already compromising.

45
00:04:04,065 --> 00:04:14,871
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you will be... even with all the reflections and all the thinking, all the right things, the time will come when it's just going to get too much and you will then willingly give in.

46
00:04:17,263 --> 00:04:33,286
[SPEAKER_00]: You can be relaxing, you can be focusing, you can be doing this, you could be doing that, all the coping mechanisms, but the point is, none... the time will come, when things build up, none of that will work, and the only reason you're not failing is because there's nothing for you to... to... to give in to.

47
00:04:33,346 --> 00:04:33,927
[SPEAKER_00]: It's too far.

48
00:04:35,007 --> 00:04:42,068
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, by the time you were to... to reach things you give in to, eh... the mind would have changed, and then you wouldn't...

49
00:04:42,128 --> 00:04:42,888
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, passed.

50
00:04:43,929 --> 00:04:44,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Especially in the beginning.

51
00:04:44,989 --> 00:04:45,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Especially in the beginning.

52
00:04:47,374 --> 00:05:04,888
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you really need to recognize that environment and foresee when your mind is leading you in that direction, when you're gradually giving in, and then just prevent yourself from ending up in that environment where you have a quick access to things that would compromise the precepts.

53
00:05:08,331 --> 00:05:13,375
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it says, it comes down to that physical separation.

54
00:05:13,983 --> 00:05:15,784
[SPEAKER_00]: So, things are further removed.

55
00:05:16,364 --> 00:05:18,245
[SPEAKER_00]: Access to entertainment is further removed.

56
00:05:18,445 --> 00:05:18,585
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

57
00:05:18,645 --> 00:05:31,709
[SPEAKER_00]: Access to things that provoke you to act with lust or anger are further removed when the crisis sets in, and that will actually provide you some... well, that will prevent you from falling back as far as you would have otherwise.

58
00:05:32,970 --> 00:05:39,152
[SPEAKER_00]: And that needs to be developed beforehand, recognizing the little signs and features that lead up towards it.

59
00:05:39,612 --> 00:05:41,813
[SPEAKER_00]: But if that's been carefully sort of

60
00:05:43,339 --> 00:05:50,243
[SPEAKER_00]: Tailored, shaped, pushed away a bit beforehand, then that will offer you some space.

61
00:05:52,484 --> 00:06:03,070
[SPEAKER_01]: But... and... so you've... you've got that space, those normal... those common things you don't have access to anymore.

62
00:06:04,371 --> 00:06:06,072
[SPEAKER_01]: But you still have access to your body.

63
00:06:06,572 --> 00:06:07,813
[SPEAKER_01]: You still have access to your mind.

64
00:06:07,893 --> 00:06:08,053
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

65
00:06:08,854 --> 00:06:09,494
[SPEAKER_01]: So you're thinking.

66
00:06:09,534 --> 00:06:10,174
[SPEAKER_01]: So... Yeah.

67
00:06:11,395 --> 00:06:12,876
[SPEAKER_01]: That you can't run away from.

68
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:13,658
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

69
00:06:13,798 --> 00:06:18,141
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's like, those things you should be developing before it gets too much.

70
00:06:19,022 --> 00:06:22,384
[SPEAKER_00]: Before the mind is too wound up with lust or anger or distraction.

71
00:06:22,444 --> 00:06:26,086
[SPEAKER_00]: Before you would have reached the point of acting out and now you're remorseful.

72
00:06:26,846 --> 00:06:37,233
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when things are fine, when you have some, as I said, some room for reflection, room for space, room for, like, discerning your intentions and contemplating them, that's which you are recognizing.

73
00:06:37,253 --> 00:06:37,533
[SPEAKER_00]: Hold on.

74
00:06:37,553 --> 00:06:37,753
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

75
00:06:37,994 --> 00:06:38,234
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

76
00:06:38,834 --> 00:06:40,035
[SPEAKER_00]: Now I'm conditionally

77
00:06:40,866 --> 00:06:48,978
[SPEAKER_00]: Temporarily safe, because the most pressing sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches that would provoke me one way or the other, are further removed.

78
00:06:49,558 --> 00:06:51,101
[SPEAKER_00]: But that doesn't mean I'm actually safe.

79
00:06:51,782 --> 00:06:53,864
[SPEAKER_00]: It just means I've kind of postponed the danger.

80
00:06:55,030 --> 00:06:55,951
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what do I do now?

81
00:06:56,031 --> 00:07:05,859
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, while I'm safe now, I should definitely be cultivating and discerning that internal relationship with my own body and my own mind.

82
00:07:06,019 --> 00:07:06,739
[SPEAKER_00]: Mind and the body.

83
00:07:06,779 --> 00:07:07,680
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how does my mind...

84
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:13,284
[SPEAKER_00]: Does my mind still regard this body as belonging to it?

85
00:07:14,545 --> 00:07:20,590
[SPEAKER_00]: Is my mind still implicitly taking the body to be the source of possible pleasure?

86
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:22,712
[SPEAKER_00]: Pleasure that is worthy to pursue?

87
00:07:23,971 --> 00:07:30,019
[SPEAKER_00]: Is my mind forgetting the lack of safety that's inherent in this physical form and the body?

88
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,383
[SPEAKER_00]: So, those contemplations, that's when you do them.

89
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:38,711
[SPEAKER_00]: When the mind is just completely wild, doesn't want to listen to you, then you just need a physical separation until it calms down.

90
00:07:39,512 --> 00:07:40,414
[SPEAKER_00]: None of this will work.

91
00:07:42,072 --> 00:07:50,517
[SPEAKER_00]: But of course, yes, if you invest the right effort before the mind winds up itself way too much, it might not wind up... wind itself up that much.

92
00:07:50,817 --> 00:08:03,884
[SPEAKER_00]: Because these perceptions that you're providing for the mind, unknown ability of the body, knowing your intentions, the danger, foreseeing the environment that could compromise you, all of that, it's kind of telling right things to that mind.

93
00:08:03,904 --> 00:08:05,725
[SPEAKER_00]: It's showing it, okay, you know,

94
00:08:06,341 --> 00:08:10,323
[SPEAKER_00]: This is better for you as well, and you will get to see it for yourself.

95
00:08:10,904 --> 00:08:19,189
[SPEAKER_00]: The animal will see for itself that, actually, this is actually better than giving in to thirst, passion, anger, distraction, entertainment.

96
00:08:19,249 --> 00:08:20,250
[SPEAKER_01]: Delighting in the body.

97
00:08:20,290 --> 00:08:21,330
[SPEAKER_00]: Delighting in the body, yeah.

98
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:31,216
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, if you are developing that right perspective in regard to your body, while you're not kind of acutely pressured, then you get to discern as well.

99
00:08:31,276 --> 00:08:32,237
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so mentally,

100
00:08:33,392 --> 00:08:41,378
[SPEAKER_00]: When images and thoughts of sensuality, or ill-will, or cruelty, how the suttas say, or conceit, they come up.

101
00:08:42,779 --> 00:08:44,841
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same sense, Sādhānsa Maltese touches come up.

102
00:08:45,861 --> 00:08:47,022
[SPEAKER_00]: But, am I accepting them?

103
00:08:47,803 --> 00:08:49,344
[SPEAKER_00]: Do I just feel like, oh, I just...

104
00:08:49,784 --> 00:08:51,206
[SPEAKER_00]: They're mine as soon as they come up.

105
00:08:51,926 --> 00:08:52,426
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is that?

106
00:08:53,027 --> 00:08:57,590
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's when you could then introduce that layer of mental purification.

107
00:09:00,438 --> 00:09:01,959
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's also what's going to shift.

108
00:09:02,259 --> 00:09:05,321
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, like, initially, people's restraint will be mechanical.

109
00:09:05,341 --> 00:09:06,783
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just going to be saying no to stuff.

110
00:09:07,703 --> 00:09:09,685
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's... that's not even the right restraint.

111
00:09:09,765 --> 00:09:10,826
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just how you have to start.

112
00:09:10,906 --> 00:09:11,146
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

113
00:09:11,886 --> 00:09:12,787
[SPEAKER_00]: But, yes, once you...

114
00:09:13,147 --> 00:09:17,771
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, you said no to certain things, to certain environments, to certain compromising situations.

115
00:09:18,091 --> 00:09:18,692
[SPEAKER_00]: You foresee them.

116
00:09:18,732 --> 00:09:19,312
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't give in.

117
00:09:19,372 --> 00:09:20,073
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't go there.

118
00:09:20,945 --> 00:09:25,727
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, by recognizing, okay, so now there is the internal relationship with this body.

119
00:09:25,887 --> 00:09:27,687
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it taken through the sense of ownership?

120
00:09:27,807 --> 00:09:29,328
[SPEAKER_00]: Taken as a basis of pleasure?

121
00:09:29,868 --> 00:09:32,149
[SPEAKER_00]: Taken as a basis of safety, mastery, control?

122
00:09:32,729 --> 00:09:34,509
[SPEAKER_00]: That's already now the right restraint.

123
00:09:34,589 --> 00:09:39,591
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, that restraint is now really not anymore like restraint, in that blind mechanical manner.

124
00:09:40,191 --> 00:09:42,312
[SPEAKER_00]: It's already a way of purification.

125
00:09:43,723 --> 00:09:45,665
[SPEAKER_00]: That's when the restraint becomes purification.

126
00:09:46,326 --> 00:09:46,867
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, same.

127
00:09:46,947 --> 00:10:00,662
[SPEAKER_00]: You recognize what thoughts are coming up, what thoughts are enduring, what thoughts are sort of persisting, what thoughts... well, what thoughts are kind of indicating the state of the animal, the state of the mind, the state of the citta.

128
00:10:01,543 --> 00:10:04,246
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you wouldn't have thoughts of anger

129
00:10:05,475 --> 00:10:27,752
[SPEAKER_00]: Coming up and besetting you, images associated with such thoughts, if the mind is not angry, if the mind is not, at least to some degree, irritated, or, or resistant, doesn't matter how ambiguous that mood might be, you could get to discern, okay, so if these are thoughts that are evolving, it's because mind is kind of leaning in that direction.

130
00:10:27,792 --> 00:10:28,432
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what do you do?

131
00:10:28,953 --> 00:10:34,017
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I need to show the animal, I need to, I need to show it that this is not beneficial.

132
00:10:34,922 --> 00:10:39,186
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can't stop the thoughts, but you could then, as we said before, okay, I will not welcome it.

133
00:10:39,246 --> 00:10:40,888
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, these thoughts keep coming up.

134
00:10:40,928 --> 00:10:42,289
[SPEAKER_00]: I won't allow them to enter the stage.

135
00:10:42,349 --> 00:10:43,190
[SPEAKER_00]: I won't welcome them.

136
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:51,257
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's already, you see, although it's still like you're restraining the allowance, the delight towards the thoughts, really, you're already purifying.

137
00:10:51,278 --> 00:10:56,943
[SPEAKER_00]: You're already sending a message to the animal that's much more than just restraint.

138
00:10:57,343 --> 00:10:59,005
[SPEAKER_00]: That's much more than just saying no.

139
00:11:00,707 --> 00:11:11,456
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the sole reason the animal is still wild is because you were welcoming such thoughts, welcoming the root of the problem, welcoming the sense of ownership, lust, aversion, whatever.

140
00:11:11,776 --> 00:11:17,201
[SPEAKER_00]: When these thoughts come up, you don't see an option for them to not be delighted in.

141
00:11:18,442 --> 00:11:22,626
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's also why people fall into the trap of trying to deny or replace thoughts.

142
00:11:22,686 --> 00:11:24,027
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't see the mind behind it.

143
00:11:26,471 --> 00:11:28,052
[SPEAKER_00]: Any thought is not a problem in itself.

144
00:11:28,172 --> 00:11:31,956
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a problem of the state of the mind of the animal that's implicit in it.

145
00:11:33,197 --> 00:11:38,161
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why, if your sole concern is to replace the thoughts, the the state of the animal doesn't change.

146
00:11:39,382 --> 00:11:41,664
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you haven't even seen it to begin with.

147
00:11:41,684 --> 00:11:50,391
[SPEAKER_00]: So, say mind is angry, you start having thoughts and then, as a result of that, you want to replace those thoughts and think positive thoughts on account of an angry mind.

148
00:11:51,852 --> 00:11:52,252
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's it.

149
00:11:52,693 --> 00:11:55,135
[SPEAKER_00]: And you have not seen the actual... you have not conveyed

150
00:11:56,010 --> 00:11:58,791
[SPEAKER_00]: The message that the mind, the animal, the citta can understand.

151
00:12:01,373 --> 00:12:11,417
[SPEAKER_00]: But, if such thoughts are coming up, or thoughts of sensuality... You can't have thoughts of sensuality if the mind is not leaning towards delighting and craving the sensual pleasures.

152
00:12:11,958 --> 00:12:13,899
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's not your problem directly.

153
00:12:13,939 --> 00:12:15,159
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not that you are doing that.

154
00:12:15,299 --> 00:12:16,680
[SPEAKER_00]: You're a victim of it, in a way.

155
00:12:17,861 --> 00:12:22,603
[SPEAKER_00]: But, given that it's just you and the mind, whether you're a victim or not, on paper,

156
00:12:23,718 --> 00:12:24,861
[SPEAKER_00]: You are the one who pays the price.

157
00:12:25,202 --> 00:12:27,107
[SPEAKER_00]: So you want to start taking responsibility of it.

158
00:12:27,127 --> 00:12:28,129
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, I'm not doing this.

159
00:12:28,250 --> 00:12:29,152
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the mind doing it.

160
00:12:29,653 --> 00:12:31,839
[SPEAKER_00]: But it doesn't absolve me from tolerating it.

161
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:33,042
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the point.

162
00:12:35,177 --> 00:12:38,098
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's only me that's going to be affected by this.

163
00:12:38,138 --> 00:12:39,538
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, I won't tolerate it.

164
00:12:40,018 --> 00:12:41,039
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how you not tolerate it?

165
00:12:41,059 --> 00:12:45,720
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, when sensual thoughts are coming up, you recognize, okay, so the mind is sensual.

166
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:55,123
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if the sensual thoughts stop coming up, even if you replace them with whatever, you still know, hold on, but those thoughts wouldn't have come up if the animal is not already wanting that.

167
00:12:56,563 --> 00:13:02,105
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even if you replace the thoughts or not, it was not about the thoughts, it was about the state of the mind behind it.

168
00:13:03,625 --> 00:13:12,567
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's why it's like, okay, so when these thoughts are coming up, I won't just blindly welcome them, accept them, try to get rid of them, or indulge them, even worse.

169
00:13:13,467 --> 00:13:16,608
[SPEAKER_00]: I will not lose the sight of the mind behind it.

170
00:13:18,609 --> 00:13:28,631
[SPEAKER_00]: And as I said before, when those thoughts are coming up, in regards to sensuality and ill-will, you already know where they would lead, what those thoughts will crystallize towards.

171
00:13:30,992 --> 00:13:32,772
[SPEAKER_00]: So the point is then just like, okay, so

172
00:13:34,356 --> 00:13:43,381
[SPEAKER_00]: There is the inclination to allow thoughts that will become sensual, to allow thoughts that will become ill-will, or conceit, or cruelty, or any associated with any hindrance.

173
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:44,702
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I won't do.

174
00:13:45,662 --> 00:13:52,266
[SPEAKER_00]: By not allowing that that last drop, last focus on, aha, this is the thought, I'm taking it up.

175
00:13:53,607 --> 00:13:58,329
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally, by unfocusing from that degree, you are staying on the level where your mind is.

176
00:13:58,610 --> 00:14:00,270
[SPEAKER_00]: You are staying with the level where the animal is.

177
